WEBVTT

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:11.513
Some things need a yes before they go ahead: a purchase, time off, access to a system, or a new procedure. In this video, you’ll ask for approval, and decide on a request.

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:22.136
Open Approvals. Every request shows its type, who decides, and the stage it’s at. Filter by type, or by open, approved, rejected and withdrawn.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:28.957
To ask for one, click New Approval. Give it a name, choose its type, and pick who decides, plus any reviewers.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:37.912
You can link a Knowledge Center page too, so the person deciding has the details in front of them. Create it, and it starts in the type’s first stage.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:45.471
Whoever decides can change the stage right from the list. Approve the grinder, and Worklynq records the date it was approved.

00:00:45.933 --> 00:00:53.720
Each request keeps an activity log of who created it, and who moved it. And every one ends approved, rejected, or withdrawn.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:01:02.060
A document approval linked to a Knowledge Center page decides whether that page shows as verified, so your team knows what’s been checked.
